msgid "For SNMPv2 and SNMPv3 Devices, the SNMP Bulk Walk max-repetitions size. The default is to 'Auto Detect on Re-Index'. For very large switches, high performance servers, Jumbo Frame Networks or for high latency WAN connections, increasing this value may increase poller performance. More data is packed into a single SNMP packet which can reduce data query run time. However, some devices may completely refuse to respond to packets with a max-repetition size which is set too large. This can be especially true for lower-powered IoT type devices or smaller embedded IT appliances. Special attention to the overall network path MTU should also be considered since setting a value which is too high could lead to packet fragmentation."
msgstr "Kwizixhobo ze-SNMPv2 neze-SNMPv3, ubungakanani be-max-repetitions ye-SNMP Bulk Walk. Okumiselweyo kukuthi 'Chonga ngokuzenzekelayo xa kuPhindwa uku-Indeksa'. Kwiiswitshi ezinkulu kakhulu, iiseva ezinamandla aphezulu, iinethiwekhi ze-Jumbo Frame okanye uqhagamshelo lwe-WAN olunolindelo olude, ukonyusa eli xabiso kunokunyusa ukusebenza kwe-poller. Idatha eninzi ipakishwa kwiphakhethi enye ye-SNMP nto leyo enokunciphisa ixesha lokusebenza kombuzo wedatha. Nangona kunjalo, ezinye izixhobo zingala ngokupheleleyo ukuphendula iiphakhethi ezinobungakanani be-max-repetition obumiselwe phezulu kakhulu. Oku kungaba yinyani ngakumbi kwizixhobo zohlobo lwe-IoT ezinamandla asezantsi okanye izixhobo ze-IT ezincinci ezifakwe ngaphakathi. Ingqalelo ekhethekileyo kwi-MTU yendlela yonke yenethiwekhi nayo kufuneka ithathelwe ingqalelo kuba ukuseta ixabiso eliphezulu kakhulu kunokukhokelela ekwahlukana kweepakhethi."

